High-Speed Connectivity Supports Automotive Imaging

Serializer-deserializer technology converts and transmits data between automotive cameras and vehicle computing systems. GMSL and FPD-Link are established technologies used to carry high-speed video and related control information across automotive cable connections.

As camera resolutions and vehicle computing requirements increase, reliable data transmission becomes more important to system performance.

ADAS Adoption Increases Camera Connectivity Requirements

Modern vehicles use cameras for forward monitoring, rear visibility, surround-view systems and driver monitoring. Higher camera counts increase the need for bandwidth, diagnostics, cable reliability and electromagnetic compatibility.

Automotive manufacturers also consider long-term product availability, qualification requirements and system integration when selecting connectivity technologies.

